    "note": "kara par lane RESTORED 2026-08-07 (kara B-2026-08-01-33). It was withdrawn while clone_bfs_par.kara did not compile \u2014 a shared struct reachable from more than one par branch was a compile error, because even pure reads race on the non-atomic refcount. The mechanism that answers it is 'frozen': a non-counting handle to a deeply-immutable shared value, so there is no refcount traffic left to race. The gate itself is unchanged and still correct. The kara par row published before that (from a stale pre-gate binary that raced, ~0.8% SIGSEGV/SIGTRAP, kara B-2026-07-28-13) was never re-measured and is not what this row is. clone_bfs_par.kara differs from clone_bfs.kara in TWO ways, both stated in its header: an index-cursor Vec worklist instead of VecDeque+pop_front (which is what the C mirror does, and which measures within noise of the deque form on the sequential lane \u2014 181.4 vs 183.8 ms), and graph construction moved into a helper so the freeze source is uniquely bound."
